# Sensitive operations accept an MFA ceremony only inside this window.
MFA_STEP_UP_MAX_AGE=15m

# Edge budget per trusted client IP for login MFA completion. Each one-use
# transaction also has an independent five-failure database lock.
MFA_COMPLETION_RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE=10

# Comma-separated exact IPs or CIDRs whose X-Forwarded-For and X-Real-IP
# accounts honours when it attributes anonymous traffic to a client address.
#
# Empty means accounts trusts no forwarding header, so every per-IP budget
# buckets on the peer — which behind an ingress and a frontend hop is one
# pod, collapsing the anonymous budgets of a whole cell onto a single bucket.
# A cell therefore names its ingress and frontend ranges here. Empty is correct
# locally, where the peer IS the client, and a malformed entry fails the boot
# rather than silently trusting a spoofable header
# (pkg/adapters/client_ip.go, ParseTrustedProxyCIDRs).
#
# This is a DIFFERENT key from the identically named one in the `gateway` group:
# that one is auth-gateway's own edge, and a deployed gateway refuses to start
# on an empty value. accounts warns instead, because a cell may front it with
# the gateway and never expose it to forwarded traffic directly.
#
# It is declared here because accounts has read it since the per-IP budgets
# existed and no group declared it. A key a service reads but no group declares
# is inert: a composition can supply a value for a declared key and never
# declare one, so an operator who set this got no attribution and no error.
TRUSTED_PROXY_CIDRS=

# Whether the direct verify path admits an access token whose revocation status
# cannot be read. Empty — the default — denies it: a revocation store that is
# down fails CLOSED.
#
# "true" trades a revoked token's remaining TTL (3 minutes, 5 while
# impersonating) for availability through a revocation-store outage. It is for
# an operator fronting accounts directly, with no auth-gateway, and it is the
# same choice the gateway's own ext_authz check exposes as
# SIDECAR_REVOCATION_FAIL_OPEN. accounts logs a warning for the whole life of
# the process when it is on.
ACCOUNTS_REVOCATION_FAIL_OPEN=

# Whether request-time central RBAC admission hard-denies. Empty and "shadow" —
# the default — classify only; "enforce" denies. Any other value fails the boot,
# so a typo cannot leave enforcement quietly off.
RBAC_CENTRAL_ENFORCEMENT=

# accounts' database transport profile: empty keeps the platform's projected
# connection; `verified-tls` or `local-identity-proxy` selects a reviewed
# hosted-custody transport, and any other value refuses the boot
# (pkg/infra/database_transport.go). Declared because accounts reads it and a
# key no group declares is never delivered, so an operator's profile was inert.
ACCOUNTS_DATABASE_TRANSPORT=

# auth-gateway's local revocation-cache window (a duration, 0 to 30s; empty is
# its default) and whether a revocation-store error admits the token. Empty
# fails CLOSED; "true" trades a revoked token's remaining TTL for availability.
# Declared because the gateway reads both and a key no group declares is never
# delivered, so an operator's choice did nothing.
SIDECAR_REVOCATION_CACHE_TTL=
SIDECAR_REVOCATION_FAIL_OPEN=

# Refreshable device sessions have a fixed maximum lifetime, expire after an
# idle window, and are bounded per user. New logins evict the least-recently
# active device family when the cap is reached.
SESSION_ABSOLUTE_LIFETIME=168h
SESSION_IDLE_TIMEOUT=24h
SESSION_MAX_ACTIVE_DEVICES=10

# WebAuthn relying-party policy. RP ID is the registrable host (no scheme or
# port). Ceremonies use the verified Codefly frontend origin; this optional
# fallback is reserved for deployments that deliberately bypass that path.
WEBAUTHN_RP_ID=localhost
WEBAUTHN_RP_DISPLAY_NAME=SaaS Starter
WEBAUTHN_RP_ORIGINS=
